##################################################
# ====== OPTIONAL / ADDITIONAL BLOCKLISTS ======
#
# The following blocklists have been commented out for optional use.
#
# To activate any of the following lists, simply search for `##FindRemoveMe2Use#` and replace it with an empty string.
#
# These lists are more specific and can be used for precise targeting based on categories like ISPs, organizations, crawlers, etc.
#
#
#
# Please note: This method provides flexibility in managing the lists and allows you to enable only the lists you need.
#
# For example:
#
# - To enable the "Comcast" ISP blocklist, search for `##FindRemoveMe2UseISPS#` and remove it to activate the line for Comcast.
#
# - To activate Riot Games' blocklist, search for `##FindRemoveMe2UseORGS#` and remove it to enable the list.
#
# - To enable the OpenAI SearchBot blocklist, search for `##FindRemoveMe2UseCRAWLERS#` and remove the marker to activate it.
##################################################
###############################################
#
############################################
# ====== OPEN DYNAMIC BLOCK LISTS (OpenDBL) ======
# Publicly maintained blocklists that update dynamically with IP ranges associated with known threats.
# Ideal for firewalls, intrusion prevention systems, and other security appliances.
#
# Use Cases: Ingress filtering for known malicious or hostile IPs, Outbound restrictions based on suspicious activity
############################################
#
# ---- Emerging Threats: Known Compromised Hosts ----
##FindRemoveMe2UseOPENDBL#LIST_OPENDBL_ETKNOWN=https://opendbl.net/lists/etknown.list
#
# ---- TOR Exit Nodes ----
##FindRemoveMe2UseOPENDBL#LIST_OPENDBL_TOR_EXIT=https://opendbl.net/lists/tor-exit.list
#
# ---- BruteforceBlocker ----
##FindRemoveMe2UseOPENDBL#LIST_OPENDBL_BRUTEFORCE=https://opendbl.net/lists/bruteforce.list
#
# ---- Blocklist.de All ----
##FindRemoveMe2UseOPENDBL#LIST_OPENDBL_BLOCKLIST_DE_ALL=https://opendbl.net/lists/blocklistde-all.list
#
# ---- Dshield (optimized) ----
##FindRemoveMe2UseOPENDBL#LIST_OPENDBL_DSHIELD=https://opendbl.net/lists/dshield.list
#
# ---- SSL Abuse IP List (SSLBL) ----
##FindRemoveMe2UseOPENDBL#LIST_OPENDBL_SSL_ABUSE=https://opendbl.net/lists/sslblock.list
#
# ---- IPSum Level 3 (IPs appearing in 3+ blocklists) ----
##FindRemoveMe2UseOPENDBL#LIST_OPENDBL_IPSUM_LEVEL3=https://opendbl.net/lists/ipsum-level3.list
#
#
#
############################################
# ======= FIREHOL INDIVIDUAL BLOCKLISTS =======
# FIREHOL provides a large collection of curated IP blocklists designed for use in firewalls, WAFs, intrusion prevention systems, and DNS filtering.
# These feeds target various categories: malicious activity, anonymity networks, brute force, spam, abuse, malware, proxies, Tor nodes, crypto mining, and more.
#
# Documentation: https://github.com/firehol/blocklist-ipsets/blob/master/README.md
############################################
#
# ---- META LEVELS (PRIMARY CURATED SETS) ----
